Mini Project Start
Project Name:
Product Review Sentiment Analyzer – E-commerce
Dataset:
Amazon Product Reviews Dataset (10,000 reviews)
Features (X Columns):
1.	Review Text 
2.	Review Length (number of words/characters) 
3.	Verified Purchase Status 
4.	Product Rating (1–5 stars) 
Target (y Column):
Sentiment Category
•	Positive 
•	Neutral 
•	Negative 
Question the Model Will Answer:
Given a customer's product review, can the model automatically determine whether the sentiment expressed is Positive, Neutral, or Negative?
________________________________________
Project Overview
M1: Data Preparation & Exploration
•	Load 10,000 Amazon reviews 
•	Perform text cleaning: 
o	Lowercasing 
o	Remove punctuation 
o	Remove special characters 
o	Remove stopwords using NLTK 
•	Explore review rating distribution 
•	Visualize sentiment and rating trends 
M2: Machine Learning Model
•	Convert review text into numerical features using TF-IDF Vectorizer 
•	Train a Naive Bayes Classifier 
•	Predict: 
o	Positive 
o	Neutral 
o	Negative 
•	Save trained model as: 
o	sentiment_model.pkl 
o	tfidf_vectorizer.pkl 
M3: Web Application
•	Build a Flask application 
•	User pastes a review into a form 
•	Display: 
o	Predicted sentiment 
o	Confidence percentage 
o	Highlighted words contributing to prediction 
M4: Deployment
•	Deploy application online 
•	Generate live URL 
•	Demonstrate sentiment prediction with sample reviews 
________________________________________
Technology Stack:
